From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jbuck2005 <59450931+jbuck2005@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:59:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] misc: armchina-npu: update to CIX NPU driver 6.2.0

The Sky1 series carries an old CIX build of the Arm China Zhouyi driver
(KMD 1.0.0). Its ioctl ABI (32 ASID bases in struct aipu_cap, no exec_id
or DMA-buf bind/rebind) does not match any current user-mode library:
Arm China's open libaipudrv 4.1.0 and CIX's NOE 3.1.2 both expect the
CIX 6.x driver ABI.

Replace the common driver and the Zhouyi v1/v2/v3 back ends with CIX's
6.2.0 release (cixtech/cix_opensource__npu_driver, branch
cix_mainline_dev, GPL-2.0), which is Arm China's 4.1.0 driver with a Sky1
layer. v3_1 is gone upstream and v3_2 is added (Kconfig renamed to
match); Sky1 is v3.

sky1/sky1.c is CIX's 6.2.0 file with the Sky1 series' mainline changes
kept:
- DVFS goes through the OPP core (dev_pm_opp_set_rate) instead of
  reaching into the SCMI perf genpd's private struct, and the OPPs come
  from the genpd's attach_dev callback instead of a direct SCMI call.
- Under ACPI the "perf" domain is attached by index with
  genpd_dev_pm_attach_by_id(), since dev->pm_domain is already the ACPI
  power-resource domain.
CIX's newer probe error unwinding, per-core teardown and core-count
update are kept.

The KMD_VERSION reported to user space is 6.2.0. No firmware is needed.
